<h2>Multiplication and Division PLC Activity</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Interpret representations of the relationship between multiplication and division. Represent the relationship between multiplication and division.</p>
<p>Warm-up Which One Doesn&#x27;t Belong: Multiplication and Division. Four original pictures A–D need teacher visual review; plausible labels alone do not determine which one is different, and more than one justified choice may be correct.</p>
<h3>Which One Doesn&#x27;t Belong?</h3><p>Use the original teacher-supplied A–D drawings and defend a choice; original figure pixels are not verified. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Card Sort: Find the Match</h3><p>Match equivalent equation/diagram cards with a classmate, then prepare a poster with a new diagram and division story. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Find the Match Gallery Walk</h3><p>Visit partner posters and justify an additional representation and a multiplication–division relationship. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<p>Original public source lesson: <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-10/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2021 teacher material</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Original-source limitation:</strong> Original publisher equation/diagram cards and A–D warm-up images were not inspected. Publisher-gated Cool-down is not claimed.</p></section>
